      ],
      "text": "**If their school is open today, keeping them home is a reasonable choice—especially if either child has asthma, another breathing condition, or haze symptoms.** Kuala Lumpur’s official API readings were around **160–163 at 11:00 a.m. MYT on Saturday, October 17**—in the unhealthy range. ([hazemonitor.com](https://hazemonitor.com/?utm_source=openai))\n\nThat reading is below the government’s current **school-closure threshold of API above 200**, but the Education Minister has said parents may keep children home if worried about their health, as long as they notify the school. Outdoor activities should be stopped once API exceeds 100. ([web26.bernama.com](https://web26.bernama.com/en/general/news.php?id=2620854&utm_source=openai))\n\nIf they do go, ask the school to keep them indoors and skip outdoor play or sports; check the latest API near your home and school before leaving, since readings can change. If a child is wheezing or struggling to breathe, keep them home and seek medical advice.",
